    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "True or False? Let $A$ and $B$ be sets in a universal set $U$.\n\n$A\\cap\\overline B=B\\cap\\overline A$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "False.",
      "worked": "False. The left side contains elements in $A$ only; the right contains elements in $B$ only. For $U=\\{1\\}$, $A=\\{1\\}$ and $B=\\varnothing$,\n$$\\begin{align*}A\\cap\\overline B&=\\{1\\},\\\\B\\cap\\overline A&=\\varnothing.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
